{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<div>The proposed development would create additional nuisance to the surroundings, including noise and fumes/odours given the proposed use as a shisha lounge. The open roof configuration/layout of the rear area of the site would inevitably create additional neighbouring impacts on the residential units on the upper levels of the terrace row, which is not considered acceptable from the neighbouring amenity perspective. The proposals would therefore constitute unneighbourly development and contrary to:<br></div><div><br></div><div><p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \" pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\">-\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework </span>(NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)<o:p></o:p></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \" pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\">- Policies D4, D6, D13 and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021); and</span><o:p></o:p></p><p><span pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\" style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">-\r\nPolicies SP2, DMD1 and DMSI3 of t</span>he London Borough of Barking and\r\nDagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024).</p></div>"
  ],
